      "dom_id": "question-156127",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "What is the solution to the following system of inequalities?\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}n+2<5 \\\\ 1-2n\\le 3\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "To solve the system, we need to find the values of $n$ that satisfy both $n+2<5$ and $1-2n\\le 3$ simultaneously.\n\n- First, we solve $n+2<5\\,:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n+2 & <5 \\\\ n+2-2 & <5-2 \\\\ n & <3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14249179/assets/4e6e1c1a65abf5b7b88d39bb4d2606d64d5bc9ae526925e9f869eab0927194e3.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n- Then, we solve $1-2n\\le 3\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-2n & \\le 3 \\\\ 1-2n-1 & \\le 3-1 \\\\ -2n & \\le 2 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-2n) & \\ge (-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\ 2n & \\ge -2 \\\\ \\frac{2n}{2} & \\ge \\frac{-2}{2} \\\\ n & \\ge -1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14249179/assets/8e96c91b84e3c69b2e8f58251dbe21294ef8b23ffa695c1b7fbe53ad4f22b2fc.png)\n\nTo find the values of $n$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14249179/assets/cd1d2ad0e357eb3117e5b61351afeda01a348bfff5aec1a2d2940c77ecae120c.png)\n\n \n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nThus, the final solution is $n\\in [-1,3).$",
