      "name": null,
      "problem": "Find the set of values of $x$ that satisfy $1<2x-1\\le 5$ and $1-2x\\le 3.$",
      "worked_solution": "To solve compound \"and\" inequalities, we solve each inequality separately and then find their intersection.\n\n- First, we solve $1<2x-1\\le 5\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & <2x-1\\le 5 \\\\ 1+1 & <2x-1+1\\le 5+1 \\\\ 2 & <2x\\le 6 \\\\ \\frac{2}{2} & <\\frac{2x}{2}\\le \\frac{6}{2} \\\\ 1 & <x\\le 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14249179/assets/2b111554de3019b78a3d6e8992477bb1401a53d7c2bbe09a6407e675b8d06daa.png)\n\n- Then, we solve  $1-2x\\le 3\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-2x & \\le 3 \\\\ 1-2x-1 & \\le 3-1 \\\\ -2x & \\le 2 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-2x) & \\ge (-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\ 2x & \\ge -2 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{2} & \\ge \\frac{-2}{2} \\\\ x & \\ge -1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14249179/assets/ca4d8a229772ec9d22a45c99cdad22379b6b55aa5d6fe4bb6288fe66d8c5696a.png)\n\nTo find the values of $x$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14249179/assets/74cc11cbd20e5b82171d4c89407f24eb6f60ee558bf41a313009839c6f885f7e.png)\n\n \n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nThus, the final solution is $x\\in (1,3].$",
